          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Lie groupoid
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
          %p
            Regarded in the more general context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoids"} smooth groupoids
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+stacks"} smooth stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
          %h2#definition Definition
          #ExplicitDefinition.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em Lie groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∶−
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇉
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \coloneq (X_1 \rightrightarrows X_0)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              such that both the space of arrows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              and the space of objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
              are smooth manifolds, all structure maps are smooth, and source and target maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇉
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s, t: X_1\rightrightarrows X_0
              are surjective submersions.
          %p
            A
            %em Lie groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            does not have all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \times_{s,t} X_1
            of composable
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoid"} internal groupoid
            in the sense of Ehresmann, which includes as data the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composable+pairs"} composable pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t : X_0 \to X_1
            are
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            exists to define said manifold of composable pairs. Therefore a definition used in most modern differential geometry literature is as we see above.
          %p
            But for most practical purposes, the apparently evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd(Diff)
            of such internal groupoids,
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functor"} internal functor
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %em not
            the correct 2-category to consider. One way to see this is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            fails in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            of internal groupoids which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            may nevertheless not be an equivalence, in that it may not have a weak inverse in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd(Diff)
          %p
            See the section
            %a{:href => "#2CatOfGrpds"} 2-Category of Lie groupoids
            below.
          %p
            A bit more general than a Lie groupoid is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoid"} diffeological groupoid
          %h3#examples_for_lie_groupoids Examples for Lie groupoids
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is a Lie groupoid with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1=G
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi pt
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=pt
                a point. Composition of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is provided by the multiplication of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              %p
                A manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is a Lie groupoid with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1=M
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=M
            %li
              %p
                Given a manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                and an open cover
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mo ⊔
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi M
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1=\sqcup U_i\times_M U_j
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⊔
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=\sqcup U_i
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi ij
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi M
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_{ij}:=(x_i, x_j)\in U_i\times_M U_j \subset X_1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi ij
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(x_{ij})=x_i \in U_i
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi ij
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(x_{ij})=x_j \in U_j
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi ij
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi jk
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi ik
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_{ij} \cdot x_{jk}= x_{ik}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+groupoid"} Čech groupoid
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong covering groupoid
            %li
              %p
                Given a Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                (right) action on a manifold
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
                (or sometimes called
                = succeed ")" do
                  %strong transformation groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi M
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 = M \times G
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=M
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, g) \in X_1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(x, g) = x
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(x, g)=x\cdot g^{-1}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, g)\cdot (y, h) = (x, g\cdot h)
                (we must have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y=x\cdot g^{-1}
                for the multiplication to happen). Action groupoid presents the quotient stack
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [M/G]
            %li
              %p
                Given a manifold
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair+groupoid"} pair groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi M
                      %mo ×
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1= M\times M
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=M
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \cdot (y , z)= (x, z)
            %li
              %p
                Given a manifold
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
                or
                %strong homotopy groupoid
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(M)
                = succeed "paths" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(M)_1=\{
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\}/
                homotopies,
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(M)=M
            %li
              %p
                Given a manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %strong>
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  \-pair groupoid
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 1
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext are in the same leaf in
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1:=\{(x, y)| x, y \;\text{are in the same leaf in}\; F \}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=M
                %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~alanw/Models.pdf"} Section 13.5 of Geometric Models for Noncommutative Algebras
                ).
            %li
              %p
                %strong
                  monodromy groupoid
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Mon
                          %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon_F(M)
                (it is a foliation version of fundamental groupoid, thus it is also sometimes called
                = succeed "-fundamental" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1:=\{
                leaf-wise paths
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \}/
                leaf-wise homotopy,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=M
                and the rest is like in the case of fundamental groupoid.
            %li
              %p
                %strong>
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+groupoid"} holonomy groupoid
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hol
                          %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hol_F(M)
                \:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1:=\{
                leaf-wise paths
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \}/
                holonomy,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0=M
                and the rest is like in the case of fundamental groupoid. Here, the holonomy of a path
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                is defined to the germ of diffeomorphisms induced by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
                between the transversals at the end points.
          %p Among all possible Lie groupoids associated to a foliation, monodromy groupoid is the biggest and holonomy groupoid is the smallest.
          %h3#terminology Terminology
          %p
            Originally Lie groupoids were called (by Ehresmann)
            %em differentiable groupoids
            (and also one considered differentiable
            = succeed ")." do
              %em categories
            %em Lie groupoid
            and
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
          %h3#specialisations Specialisations
          %p
            One definition which Ehresmann introduced in his paper
            %em Catégories topologiques et catégories différentiables
            (see below) is that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial+category"} locally trivial groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                    %mi iso
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1^{iso}
            denote the subspace (resp. submanifold) of invertible arrows . (This always exists, by general abstract nonsense - I should look up the reference, it’s in Bunge-Pare I think -
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"} DR
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A topological groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⇉
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \rightrightarrows X_0
              is
              %strong locally trivial
              if for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in X_0
              there is a neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              and a lift of the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p\} \times U \hookrightarrow X_0 \times X_0
              through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                        %mi iso
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t):X_1^{iso}\to X_0 \times X_0
          %p
            Clearly for a Lie groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                      %mi iso
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1^{iso} = X_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t)
            has local sections. Ehresmann goes on to show a link between smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            and transitive, locally trivial Lie groupoids. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial+category"} locally trivial category
            for details.
          %h3#2CatOfGrpds The (2,1)-category of Lie groupoids
          %p
            As usual for internal categories, the naive 2-category of internal groupoids,
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functor"} internal functor
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            fails in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            so that an internal functor which is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            may still not have an internal weak inverse.
          %p
            One way to deal with this is to equip the 2-category with some structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            and allow morphisms of Lie groupoids to be
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X \to Y
          %p
            Such generalized morphisms – called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+morphisms"} Morita morphisms
            or
            %em generalized morphisms
            in the literature – are sometimes modeled as
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bibundle"} bibundle
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilsum-Skandalis+morphism"} Hilsum-Skandalis morphism
          %p
            Another equivalent approach is to embed Lie groupoids into the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            theory:
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} (2,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(Diff)
            of
            = succeed "s/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaves"} 2-sheaves
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            may be understood as a nice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of general groupoids
            %em modeled on
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            allows to emebed groupoids internal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
            into stacks on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoid"} diffeological groupoid
          %p
            Regarded inside this wider context, Lie groupoids are identified with
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-category"} (2,1)-category
            of Lie groupoids is then the full sub-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            \-category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(Diff)
            on differentiable stacks.
          %p
            For more comments on this, see also the beginning of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
          %h2#lie_algebroid Lie algebroid
          %p
            As the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+space"} infinitesimal
            approximation to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A Lie algebroid is a vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to M
              together with a vector bundle morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi TM
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho: A\to TM
              (called anchor map), and a Lie bracket
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
              on the space of sections of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi fY
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo +
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Y
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X, fY]=f[X,Y]+\rho(X)(f) Y.
          .num_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              You would expect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              to preserve
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
            %p
              Recent progress: it turns out that one may link Lie algebroid with
              = succeed "-spaces" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %h3#examples_of_lie_algebroids Examples of Lie algebroids
          %ul
            %li
              %p A Lie algebra is a Lie algebroid with base space being a point.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                \-bundle over a manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is certainly a Lie algebroid in a trivial way.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
            %li
              %p
                Tangent bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TM
                      %mo →
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TM\to M
                is a Lie algebroid with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo =
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho=id
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
                the usual Lie bracket for vector fields. See
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
            %li
              %p
                Given a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                with Poisson bivector field
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mo *
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*P
                is equipped with a Lie algebroid structure:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\rho(\xi)=
                      \\pi(\xi)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\xi_1, \xi_2]=d\pi(\xi_1, \xi_2)
                (or you may have
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi df
                      %mo ,
                      %mi dg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [df, dg]=d\{ f, g\}
                if you prefer to think in Poisson bracket). See
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+Lie+algebroid"} Poisson Lie algebroid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+algebroid"} Atiyah Lie algebroid
          %h2#MorphismsOfLieGroupoids Morphisms of Lie groupoids
          %p There are several versions of Lie groupoid morphisms, some of them are equivalent in a correct sense, some of them are not.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                strict morphism: a strict morphism from Lie groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                is a functor from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                as categories and preserving the smooth structures.
            %li
              %p
                generalised morphism: a generalised morphism from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
                of morphisms
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mo ≃
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X \to Y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \stackrel{\simeq}{\rightarrow} X
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
                of Lie groupoids, defined as below (see also at
                = succeed ")." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bibundle"} bibundle
          %p
            A Lie groupoid functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : G\to H
            is a
            %strong weak equivalence
            if it is
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                essentially surjective; that is,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi pr
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \circ pr_2 : G_0 \times_{H_0,s} H_1 \to H_0
                is a surjective submersion;
            %li
              %p
                fully faithful; that is,
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≅
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %mo ×
                            %mi s
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_1 \cong H_1\times_{t\times s, H_0\times H_0} G_0 \times G_0
          %p
            Composition of generalised morphism is given by weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of Lie groupoids (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+limit"} weak limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X\to Y
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X' \to Y
            %strong
              weak
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X\to Y
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X' \to Y
            is a groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mi w
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \times_{Y}^w \hat X'
            with space of objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X_0 \times_{ Y_0} Y_1 \times_{Y_0} \hat X'_0
            and space of morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X_1 \times_{Y_0} Y_1 \times_{Y_0} \hat X'_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X' \to Y
            is a weak equivalence, the weak pullback is a Lie groupoid thank to the property of essentially surjective. (Is this composition associative?)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"}> anafunctor
              \: an anafunctor from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              of morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mo ≃
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X \to Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \stackrel{\simeq}{\rightarrow} X
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
              of Lie groupoids. That is, this map is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              of Lie groupoids and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X_0 \to X_0
              is a surjective submersion.
          %p
            Composition of anafunctors is given through strong
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of Lie groupoids, that is level-wise pullback.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bibundle"} bibundle
              functor (or H.S. bibundle, or Hilsum-Skandalis bibundle): a bibundle functor from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\to H
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+principal+bundle"} groupoid principal bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              (with right action) such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              acts on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              from left and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              action commutes with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              action. If both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              actions are principal, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              gives arise to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
              between them.
          %p
            The last three morphisms are more or less equivalent, that is they give arise to equivalent 2-categories (in fact (2,1)-categories) of Lie groupoids. To make it explicit, we need to talk about
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            between bibundle functors is simply a bibundle isomorphism (of course preserving all the structures of bibundles).
          %p
            A strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            from generalised morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ≃
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X \to Y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ≃
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X' \to Y
            is given by a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to \hat X'
            such that the following diagram commutes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{matrix}
                  \&amp;          &amp; \hat X \\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;           &amp; \searrow \\
                  X &amp;          &amp; \downarrow &amp;          &amp; Y \\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;           &amp; \swarrow \\
                  \&amp;          &amp; \hat X'
                  \\end{matrix}
          %p
            This forces the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to \hat X'
            to be a weak equivalence by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
            for weak equivalences. A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ≃
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X \to Y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ≃
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ′
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X' \to Y
            is provided by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            of strict 2-morphisms:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ″
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{matrix}
                  \&amp;          &amp; \hat X \\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;     \uparrow      &amp; \searrow \\
                  X &amp;          &amp; \hat X'' &amp;          &amp; Y \\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;       \downarrow    &amp; \swarrow \\
                  \&amp;          &amp; \hat X'
                  \\end{matrix}
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
            between
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
            = succeed "?)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to \hat X'
          %p
            Then these three (2,1)-categories, which we denote by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GEN
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GEN
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ANA
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ANA
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BUN
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BUN
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalent"} equivalent
            to each other. For a nice survey on this statement, we refer to Section 1.5 of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ediss.uni-goettingen.de/handle/11858/00-1735-0000-0022-5F4F-A"} Du Li’s thesis
          %p
            The idea is that
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/bibundle#bundlisation"} Bundlisation
            may extend to an equivalence of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GEN
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GEN
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BUN
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BUN
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E: G\to H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            along the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\to G_0
            and obtain a Lie groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi E
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 0
                    %mi E
                    %mo ×
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G|_E:=G_1\times_{G_0\times G_0} E \times E \Rightarrow E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G|_E \to G
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to H
          %p
            Even though
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GEN
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GEN
            contains more morphisms than
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ANA
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ANA
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ≃
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \hat X \to Y
            gives arise to an anafunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mi w
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} X \times_{X}^w \hat X \to Y
          %p
            As a consequence of the universal property of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+fractions"} calculus of fractions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi GEN
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GEN
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ANA
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ANA
            are equivalent.
          %h2#morphisms_of_lie_algebroids Morphisms of Lie algebroids
          %p
            Morphisms of Lie algebroids are counter-intuitive: they are not morphisms of vector bundles which preserve the algebroid structure. To define a Lie algebroid morphism, we first need to introduce the
            %em Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            associated to a Lie algebroid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            We consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to be a trivially graded vector bundle, i.e. concentrated in degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[1]
            is concentrated in degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[1]
            are given as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(A[1])=C^\infty(M)\oplus \Gamma(A^*)\oplus \Gamma(\wedge^2 A^*)\oplus \ldots ,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(M)
            is considered to be of degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(A^*)
            to be of degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            Now we can define a degree-one derivation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(A[1])
            as follows: For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \in \Gamma(\wedge^n A^*)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i\in \Gamma(A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi …
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi i
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi j
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mi j
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi …
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %mo ^
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi …
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %mo ^
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo +
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi …
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %mo ^
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_A(\xi)(X_1,\,\ldots\,,\,X_n) := \sum_{0\leq i \lt j\leq n} (-1)^{i+j} \xi\bigl([X_i,\,X_j]_A,\, \ldots\,,\, \widehat{X_i},\,\ldots\,,\,\widehat{X_i},\,\ldots\bigr) + \sum_{i=0}^n (-1)^i \rho_A(X_i) \xi\bigl(\ldots\,,\,\widehat{X_i},\,\ldots\bigr).
          %p
            The condition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [d_A,\,d_A] = 0
            is not automatically fulfilled: since
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \deg d_A = 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [d_A,\,d_A] = d_A \circ d_A + d_A \circ d_A = 2 d_A \circ d_A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_A \circ d_A = 0
            is actually equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigl(A, \rho_A, [ - , - ]_A\bigr)
            being a Lie algebroid; that is, it is fulfilled if and only if
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [- , - ]_A
              satisfies the Jacobi identity
            %li
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [ - , - ]_A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_A
              together satisfy the Leibniz identity.
          %p
            (Proof: calculation gives the restriction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_A(f) = \rho^\ast(d f)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_A(\xi)(X_1, X_2)
                  \= - \bigl\langle \xi, [X_1, X_2]\bigr\rangle
                  + \rho_A(X_1)(\xi X_2) - \rho_A(X_2)(\xi X_1)
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_A(\xi)(X_1, X_2, X_3)
                    \= - \xi([X_1, X_2], X_3) + \xi([X_1, X_3], X_2) - \xi([X_2, X_3], X_2)
                    + \rho_A(X_1)\xi(X_2, X_3) - \rho_A(X_2)\xi(X_1, X_3) + \rho_A(X_3)\xi(X_1, X_2)
          %p
            This point of view also applies to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Courant+Lie+algebroids"} higher Courant Lie algebroids
            and
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebra"} L-infinity-algebra
          %p
            Example: For the tangent Lie algebroid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi T
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = T M
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigl(C(T M[1]), d_A\bigr) = \bigl(\Omega^\ast(M), d_{dR}\bigr)
          %p
            Then a morphism from a Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \rho_A, [-,-]_A)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B, \rho_B, [-,-]_B)
            is a morphism of the associated differential graded commutative algebras
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (C(A[1]), d_A) \leftarrow (C(B[1]), d_B).
          %p
            Such a morphism of c.d.g.a.‘s is determined by maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(N) \to C^\infty (M)
            on degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(B^*)\to \Gamma(A^*)
            on degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\xrightarrow{f} B
            give rise to a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            of c.g.a. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to be a Lie algebroid morphism, we further need
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to satisfy additional conditions so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            preserves the differential.
          %p
            This way to explain morphisms of Lie algebroids is described in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Mackenzie"} Kirill Mackenzie
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            can be described as a morphism of vector bundles that respects the anchor maps and the Lie bracket. If, however,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is over a different manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            (Note that this is not simply the vector bundle pullback of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            along
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Mackenzie"} Kirill Mackenzie
          %h3#example Example
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            be an interval with the tangent bundle Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi TI
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %mi TI
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (TI, \id_{TI}, [-,-])
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \rho_A, [-,-]_A)
            an arbitrary Lie algebroid on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\colon I \to A
            defines a map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi TI
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi\colon C(A[1]) \to C(TI[1]) \cong \Omega(I)
            which respects the commutative graded algebra structure. A function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\in C^{\infty}(M)
            gets mapped to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ \gamma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma\colon I \to M
            is the projection of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in\Gamma(A^*)
            gets mapped to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi dt
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s\circ \gamma (a) dt
            under
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dt
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dt
            is the canonical section of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(I)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi TI
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(TI[1])
            is concentrated in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %p
            For this map to be a morphism of Lie algebroids, it has to respect the differentials. As explained above this only needs to be checked for a smooth function in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\infty}(M)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\varphi(d_A f) = d_{dR} \varphi(f) \qquad f\in C^{\infty}(M).
          %p A quick calculation shows that this is true if and only if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mi d
                    %mi dt
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\rho_A(a(t)) = \frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t).
          %h3#example_2 Example
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            the unit square in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi TM
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                    %mi TM
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (TM, \id_{TM}, [-,-])
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo .
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, T\cdot, [-.-]_{\mathfrak{g}})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is a Lie algebra, is given by a morphism of c.d.g.a.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (CE(\mathfrak{g}), d_{\mathfrak{g}}) \to (\Omega(M), d_{dR}).
          %p
            Two smooth maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b\colon M\to \mathfrak{g}
            give a map between c.g.a. spaces above. Here a section
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in\Gamma(\mathfrak{g}^*)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^*
            gets mapped to the one form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi dt
                  %mo +
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ds
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  s(a) dt + s(b) ds,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t,s)
            are the coordinates on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mi da
                    %mi ds
                  %mo −
                  %mfrac
                    %mi db
                    %mi ds
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{da}{ds} - \frac{db}{ds} = [a,b]_{\mathfrak{g}}.
          %p
            This formula also shows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi dt
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi ds
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\cdot dt + b\cdot ds
            is a flat connection on the trivial principal
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %h3#open_problem Open problem
          %p
            It is unclear how to use the idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bibundle"} bibundle
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            to define a more general version of Lie algebroid morphisms so that they really correspond to the case of Lie groupoid morphisms.
          %h2#higher_lie_groupoids Higher Lie groupoids
          %p See
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} internal ∞-groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+groupoid"} ∞-Lie groupoid
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a 0-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-groupoid"} truncated
                Lie groupoid.
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                the one-object
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                is a Lie groupoid.
            %li
              %p
                The Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                itself is a 0-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                in the 2-category or Lie groupoids.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-group"} Lie 2-group
                is in particular a Lie groupoid: a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                in the category of Lie groupoids.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+automorphism+2-group"} inner automorphism 2-group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi E
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi INN
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}G = INN(G) = G//G
                is a Lie groupoid. There is an obvious morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi E
                        %mi G
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}G \to \mathbf{B}G
            %li
              %p
                For every
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
                there is its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+Lie+groupoid"} Atiyah Lie groupoid
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi At
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} At(P)
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(X)
                of a smooth manifold is naturally a Lie groupoid.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+groupoid"} path groupoid
                of a smooth manifold is naturally a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+groupoid"} diffeological groupoid
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(U)
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
                of a smooth manifold is a Lie groupoid.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation"} foliation
                gives rise to its
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+groupoid"} holonomy groupoid
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
                is a Lie groupoid.
            %li
              %p
                An
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} C(U) \to \mathbf{B}G
                from a smooth manifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
                in degree 1 with values in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %li
              %p
                The (1-categorical)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi P
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi E
                              %mi G
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                            %mtd
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mi G
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mo ≃
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      P &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow}&amp; \mathbf{P} &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{E}G
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; C(U) &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq}}
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; X
                      }
              %p
                is a Lie groupoid equivalent to this principal bundle
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %p
                (For more on the general phenomenon of which this is a special case see
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
                and
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} universal principal ∞-bundle
            %li
              %p
                Similarly an anafunctor from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_1(X)
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
                (see there for details).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"}> smooth groupoid
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functor"} smooth functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LieGrpd"}> LieGrpd
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothGrpd"} SmoothGrpd
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisection+of+a+Lie+groupoid"} bisection of a Lie groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+Lie+groupoid"}> effective Lie groupoid
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+Lie+groupoid"} proper Lie groupoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+groupoid"} etale groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+a+Lie+groupoid"} homotopy groups of a Lie groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+morphism"}> Morita morphism
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilsum-Skandalis+morphism"} Hilsum-Skandalis morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality+for+Lie+groupoids"} Tannaka duality for Lie groupoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+Lie+groupoid"} double Lie groupoid
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of Lie categories, hence of Lie groupoids, goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégories topologiques et categories différentiables
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EhresmannCategoriesTopologiques.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an:0205.28202"} zbMath:0205.28202
          %p
            Their understanding as
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoids"} internal groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothManifolds"} SmoothManifolds
            is often attributed to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Catégories structurées
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/ASENS_1963_3_80_4_349_0"} numdam:ASENS_1963_3_80_4_349_0
          %p
            but the simple notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+groupoids"} internal groupoids
            (
            %a{:href => "internalization#Grothendieck60"}> Grothendieck 1960
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "internalization#Grothendieck61"} 61
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Mackenzie"}> Kirill Mackenzie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie groupoids and Lie algebroids in differential geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511661839"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511661839
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=896907"} MR:896907
            %li#MoerdijkMrcun03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janez+Mr%C4%8Dun"} Janez Mrčun
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Foliations and Lie Groupoids
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615450"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511615450
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in the context of
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+theory"} foliation theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliation+groupoids"} foliation groupoids
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Mackenzie"}> Kirill Mackenzie
                ,
                %em General Theory of Lie Groupoids and Lie Algebroids,
                Cambridge University Press, 2005 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781107325883"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9781107325883
                )
          %p Historical review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Pradines"}> Jean Pradines
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  In
                  = succeed "\u2018s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann"} Ehresmann
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.1608"} arXiv:0711.1608
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.impan.pl/en/publishing-house/banach-center-publications/all/76/0/86184/in-ehresmann-s-footsteps-from-group-geometries-to-groupoid-geometries"} doi:10.4064/bc76-0-5
          %p
            Lie groupoids as a source for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry"} Noncommutative Geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.elsevier.com/books/noncommutative-geometry/connes/978-0-08-057175-1"} ISBN:9780080571751
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/docs/book94bigpdf.pdf"} pdf
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                \:
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/TWF.html"} TWF
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/week256.html"} 256
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groupoids: Unifying Internal and External Symmetry – A Tour through some Examples
                %strong 43
                7 (1996) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/199607/weinstein.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Weinstein_Groupoids.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henrique+Bursztyn"}> Henrique Bursztyn
                , Matias del Hoyo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lie Groupoids
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.14105"} arXiv:2309.14105
          %p
            Most discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            %a{:href => "orbifold#DefinitionViaProperEtaleGroupoids"} proper étale groupoids
            include a review of Lie groupoids, see the references
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#orbifold#ReferencesAsLieGroupoids"} there
          %p
            Review of the relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
          %ul
            %li#Blohmann08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Blohmann"}> Christian Blohmann
              , Section 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stacky Lie groups
              %strong 2008
              rnn082 (2008) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702399"}> arXiv:math/0702399
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/imrn/rnn082"} doi:10.1093/imrn/rnn082
          %p Groupoids and their various morphisms between them in different categories, including in Diff, is also in
          %ul
            %li
              Ralf Meyer and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              = succeed "," do
                %em Groupoids in categories with pretopology
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/pdf/1408.5220.pdf"} arXiv:math/1408.5220
